{"name":"Plantation Island","hex":"#9b8a44","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"plantation","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large farm; estate or area of land designated for agricultural growth. Often includes housing for the owner and workers.","An area where trees are planted, either for commercial purposes, or to adorn an estate."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plantation"},{"term":"island","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A contiguous area of land, smaller than a continent, totally surrounded by water.","A contiguous area of land, smaller than a continent, partially surrounded by water; a peninsula; a half-island."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To surround with water; make into an island.","To set, dot (as if) with islands."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/island"}],"entries":[{"title":"Plantation Island, Florida","blocks":[{"text":"Plantation Island is a census-designated place (CDP) in Collier County, Florida, United States. The population was 119 at the 2020 census, down from 163 at the 2010 census. It is part of the Naples–Marco Island Metropolitan Statistical Area."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Collier_County_Florida_Incorporated_and_Unincorporated_areas_Plantation_Island_Highlighted.svg/330px-Collier_County_Florida_Incorporated_and_Unincorporated_areas_Plantation_Island_Highlighted.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plantation_Island%2C_Florida","wikidata":"Q2571686"},{"title":"Malolo Lailai","blocks":[{"text":"Malolo Lailai, also known as Plantation Island, is the second largest and most developed of the Mamanuca Islands, lying 20 kilometres west of Nadi on Fiji's main island Viti Levu. Malolo Lailai is the centre of tourism in the Mamanuca Islands, and consists of four resorts, a number of residential houses, a marina and a golf course."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Malolo_Lailai.jpg/330px-Malolo_Lailai.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Malolo_Lailai","wikidata":"Q4915121"},{"title":"Plantation","blocks":[{"text":"Plantations are farms specializing in cash crops, usually mainly planting a single crop, with perhaps ancillary areas for vegetables for eating and so on. Plantations, centered on a plantation house, grow crops including cotton, cannabis, tobacco, coffee, tea, cocoa, sugar cane, opium, coca, sisal, oil seeds, oil palms, fruits, rubber trees and forest trees. Plantation crops are grown on large lands called estates. These crops are grown with scientific methods and a large, highly skilled labor force. Crops such as tea and coffee are grown on hillslopes as they cannot withstand stagnant water. Protectionist policies and natural comparative advantage have sometimes contributed to determining where plantations are located."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Los-esclavos-en-cuba-1.jpg/330px-Los-esclavos-en-cuba-1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plantation","wikidata":"Q188913"},{"title":"Island","blocks":[{"text":"An island or isle is a piece of land, distinct from a continent, completely surrounded by water. There are continental islands, which were formed by being split from a continent by plate tectonics, and oceanic islands, which have never been part of a continent. Oceanic islands can be formed from volcanic activity, grow into atolls from coral reefs, and form from sediment along shorelines, creating barrier islands. River islands can also form from sediment and debris in rivers. Artificial islands are those made by humans, including small rocky outcroppings built out of lagoons and large-scale land reclamation projects used for development."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Hawaje-NoRedLine.jpg/330px-Hawaje-NoRedLine.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Island","wikidata":"Q23442"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/VitiLevu2021OSM.png/500px-VitiLevu2021OSM.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/VitiLevu2021OSM.png/1280px-VitiLevu2021OSM.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/VitiLevu2021OSM.png/500px-VitiLevu2021OSM.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVitiLevu2021OSM.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Malolo_Lailai_Fiji.jpg/500px-Malolo_Lailai_Fiji.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Malolo_Lailai_Fiji.jpg/500px-Malolo_Lailai_Fiji.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Beach","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMalolo_Lailai_Fiji.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Malolo.jpg/500px-Malolo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Malolo.jpg/500px-Malolo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"View from pier","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMalolo.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Sugar_cane_workers_resting_1a34016v.jpg/500px-Sugar_cane_workers_resting_1a34016v.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipe